A||N||5||vinnywolfe||front exhaust manifold||||5||
Z||000000||vinnywolfe||07-05-2000||10:32 PM||||i have discovered crack all the way around my front exhaust manifold.  since i have to replace it, i figured i would put on new manifold gaskets (high temp).  i got the rear manifold off with only a slight problem.  i broke a bolt off!  fortunately, i can reach it with a small 90 degree air drill chuck and an easy out.  however, i have tried to remove the front manifold and cannot get even one bolt loose.  not only are they in there tight, but getting to them is a real pain in the a#&!  any suggestions?  i have been saturating them in penetrating oil for two days, and i cannot budge them.  but i can't really get a wrench on them squarely to apply enough torque.  are there any trick to getting out a stubborn exhaust manifold bolt?  i don't think i would be able to use any easy out on the front ones, should i break one off.<P>thanks,<P>vinnny<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||07-05-2000||11:53 PM||||Vinnywolfe, I know this is a lot of work but you could remove the head with the manifold attached to the head and then use an acetylene torch to heat the bolts red hot. When you heat the bolts red hot they come right out. If you try to heat them in the car you may end up with a pile of burnt plastic if you know what I mean.||||reg||1
Z||000002||black-86-GT||07-06-2000||12:33 AM||||I recomend going ahead taking the head off. I tried it the other way and when the wrench sliped i cut my thumb all the way down to the bone i still cant move it 100% yet. its not that hard to do just take your time with it. it can be done in a weekend. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||07-06-2000||05:06 AM||||Before you ripe down the top end of the engine have you unbolted the rear cradle bolts to hinge the engine downward? This plus taking the trunklid off will tilt that part of the engine up towards you. Don't worry, the torque strut will keep the engine from going too far. Just put the jack stands just before the front cradle bolts and hinge it down! At least if THAT doesn't work you say you tried your best!<BR>Good luck, let us know how it went!||||reg||4
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-06-2000||01:52 PM||||mine was replaced by the dealer last year under the recall, i watched some of what they did. raised the car on lift and removed the front cradle bolts and let engine assby rock down on rear bolts. they broke 3 bolts off and had to drill them out. the fix for permanent repair is to use grade 8 STUDS, NOT OEM BOLTS, with nuts. Then when you ever have to take them out even if they weld themselves in head, just the nut comes off. <P>rg||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||07-06-2000||03:38 PM||||Does anyone know what the recall number is? Is it part of the crankcase ventilation recall?<P>Both of my cars have the crankcase vent change. I just wonder if the manifold change is part of that same recall.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
